 "notes": "The colophon contains two copying records: an earlier verse recording that King Jagajjyotirmalla brought the text from Mithilā and had it copied by Viśvasiṃha Gaṇaka in Śāke 1550 (Śāke gagaṇabāṇaśaracandre = 1550, Śrāvaṇa śukla 6 Saturday c. 1628 CE), and the present copy prepared under King Jayajitāmitramalla in NS 808 during the administration of the pramāṇa Bhāgirāma. Rūpanārāyaṇa and Bhairavabhūmipāla refer to King Bhairavasiṃha of Mithilā who patronised Vācaspatimiśra.",
